    <paragraphs>
        <title>Notation and Big Assumption</title>

        <sidebyside/>
        <sidebyside widths="40% 40%" valign="top">
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <p>
                        Input variables: <m>X_1, X_2, \cdots, X_p</m>
                    </p>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <p>
                        Output variable: <m>Y</m>
                    </p>
                </li>
            </ul>

            <stack>
                <p>
                    <md>
                        Y = f(X) + \epsilon
                    </md>
                </p>

                <p component="instructor-notes">
                    <ul>
                        <li>
                            <p>
                                <m>f</m> is the systemic information that
                                <m>X</m> provides about <m>Y</m>.
                            </p>
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <p>
                                It is the ground truth that we want but can't
                                access
                            </p>
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <p>
                                So our goal is to come up with an estimated
                                model <m>\hat f</m>.
                            </p>
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <p>
                                <m>\epsilon</m> is a random error term which is
                                independent of <m>X</m> and has mean <m>0</m>
                            </p>
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </stack>
        </sidebyside>
    </paragraphs>

    <paragraphs>
        <title>Advertising Example</title>

        <image source="figures/Fig2-1.png">
            <shortdescription>
                Sales versus TV, radio, and newspaper advertising spending all
